789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051084 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051084 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051084 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051084 #edb/ref 1031 "The Chain Rule for Differentiation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051084 #edb/ref 1033 1108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051084 #edb/ref 1034 1.4416972363891276 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051084 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7fcc3a06-676a-55a2-9979-d3726053babe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064125 #edb/ref 1069 "e-732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064125 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x) = 2\\sin (3x - 1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064125 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2bb17470-6365-5e08-b649-f9f42146a4c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064125 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function\n\n$$\nf = 2\\sin u, \\qquad u=3x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = 2\\cos u, \\qquad\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064126 #edb/ref 1069 "e-733" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064126 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}$ if $y = 4\\csc (5x + 3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064126 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7f56b401-c800-5708-8978-b84ce3f542f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064126 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = 4 \\csc u, \\qquad u = 5x+3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = -4\\csc u\\cot u, \\qquad\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 5.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-20\\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u \\\\  & =-20\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+3)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064127 #edb/ref 1069 "e-734" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064127 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x) = \\sin^3{x}$, calculate $f'(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064127 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "373a63fc-3dae-5880-8a49-63b5c64888f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064127 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write\n\n$$\nf(x) = (\\sin{x})^3.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf = u^3, \\qquad u=\\sin x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = 3u^2, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\cos{x}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =3{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064129 #edb/ref 1069 "e-735" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064129 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $y = \\tan{\\left(\\sin(x)\\right)}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064129 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4ebd0289-b278-5352-b7bd-10ae218c43fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064129 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\tan u, \\qquad u = \\sin x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = \\sec^2 u,\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm d x} = \\cos x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186491422 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186491425 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186491432 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186491434 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186491436 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1039 "Differentiating a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186491440 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186064125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064281 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7