db/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064833 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "55ba3ddf-3b81-51ce-a46b-d6facbbbea67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064833 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064948 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064948 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72154" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064948 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064948 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)=9{sin}^{2}⁡(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064948 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "270b54b6-fdc6-5a75-af7c-f8052eee38ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064948 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=9(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=9{u}^{2},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=18u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =18u\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =18\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065168 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065168 #edb/ref 1061 2508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065168 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2bd9287a-2129-5eca-a08d-0604b85098f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065168 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065169 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065169 #edb/ref 1061 2509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065169 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "802f8bf9-59c4-5175-a0ca-7d35efead9be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065169 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065170 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065170 #edb/ref 1061 2511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065170 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d9287e55-1147-562c-8f80-87d0d9025112" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065170 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065171 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065171 #edb/ref 1061 2513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065171 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "be380263-f82e-517f-baaa-359929115440" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065171 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065172 #edb/ref 1061 2515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065172 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f87118f2-75ec-56c4-9391-82c2aa059a28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065172 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065335 #edb/ref 1064 "The chain rule can be used to differentiate trigonometric functions like \n\n$$\ny = \\sin (2x).\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\sin u, \\qquad u = 2x.\n$$\n\nWe can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}u)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}u\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $u=2x,$ we obtain the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\operatorname{cos}(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065335 #edb/ref 1065 1275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065335 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "40623a7d-e08a-5ec3-a3d6-1fac6307b20a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065335 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233777 #edb/ref 1069 "q-31241" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233777 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233777 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the slope of $y=\\operatorname{sin}({x}^{2}+2x-1)$ at $x=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233777 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "97de5fad-6e5e-571a-91b7-dfa67983b9d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233777 #edb/ref 1074 "The slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ is given by ${f}^{'}(0).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{'}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}u,\\,u={x}^{2}+2x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x+2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}u\\cdot (2x+2) \\\\  & =(2x+2)\\operatorname{cos}u \\\\  & =(2x+2)\\operatorname{cos}({x}^{2}+2x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(0) & =(2\\cdot 0+2)\\operatorname{cos}({0}^{2}+2\\cdot 0-1) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}(-1) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ is $2\\operatorname{cos}1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234318 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72163" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234318 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234318 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $y=\\operatorname{sin}(\\operatorname{sec}x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234318 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d3114b1b-5508-592e-9c4c-63d9fe2d48cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234318 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}u,\\,u=\\operatorname{sec}x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}u\\cdot (\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\operatorname{cos}(\\operatorname{sec}x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316268 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{csc}(x)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316268 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316268 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cb68a3a2-59aa-56c5-bc1b-c4aa4acceb78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316535 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\operatorname{csc}x\\operatorname{cot}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316535 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316535 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fd80f4fc-d66d-5918-905b-16bb0d321fbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316640 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186316535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316640 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316640 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316640 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186316535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316640 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "28742ecc-1707-5ebf-af66-6910320113a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316888 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186316268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316888 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316888 #edb/ref 107